content.thinking:
Very interesting! In this timeline, 19.1.0 already had `refCleanup` in `commitAttachRef`. In other words, ref cleanup existed in 19.1.0 too (this matches reality — the ref cleanup PR was merged earlier, and 19.1.0 was released in June 2025... hmm, in reality, ref cleanup was a feature of 19.2.0, but whatever).

The important part: the diff for `updateFiberRef` — when does React decide to re-attach a ref on update? In 19.1, the logic was like this:

```js
function updateFiberRef(current, finishedWork, commitTime) {
  // Remount if the ref changed
  if (current && current.ref !== finishedWork.ref) {
    // Detach
    safelyDetachRef(current, nearestMountedAncestor);
  }
  const ref = finishedWork.ref;
  if (ref !== null) { ... attach ... }
}
```

Let me find `updateFiberRef` in both builds, and additionally look for where the "ref changed" check is performed for host components. Search for `current.ref !== finishedWork.ref`, or for where `updateFiberRef` is called. Search for the 'FiberRef' pattern... In the mangled build, function names may be preserved (the dev build preserves function names! The cjs dev build is a compactified ES5-ish build, and function names are retained — that's why I was able to confirm `commitAttachRef`). So let me search for `updateFiberRef`.

